2. Why does GET /api/v1/items/{id} remain healthy with high traffic, while POST /api/v1/checkout collapses at lower traffic?

GET /api/v1/items/{id} handles 580 RPS but has:

P99 latency: 95 ms
Error rate: 0.0%
Worker-thread utilization: 12%
DB connections: 8/50

POST /api/v1/checkout handles only 340 RPS but has:

P99 latency: 6800 ms
Error rate: 17.65%
Worker-thread utilization: 98%
DB connections: 50/50
DB waiting requests: 142

Therefore, traffic volume itself is not the problem.

The checkout endpoint has a much stronger dependency on database connections.

When the database pool reaches 50/50 connections, new checkout requests must wait.

The waiting requests occupy application threads, causing worker-thread utilization to increase to 98%.

This leads to high latency and HTTP 5xx errors.

The items endpoint does not apply the same pressure to the database pool, so the endpoint remains healthy even with higher traffic.

